              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chéngwùyuán — \"flight attendant; cabin crew\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chéngwùyuán zhǎohuí le wǒ de shǒujī — The flight attendant found my phone for me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chéngwùyuán is built from chéng 'to ride', wù 'a task' and yuán 'a member of staff', all inherited from Middle Chinese, zying, mjuH and hjwen (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'business, affairs'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
